{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e","id":46764,"title":"What book topic would you like to see in Scion 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T23:29:22-08:00","id":46764,"title":"What book topic would you like to see in Scion 2E?","content":"So far we know the outline for the four main books (though I hope that OP will have example pantheons that could be used in Scion. I would love to see Donnie, Horace, Bridgette, Himiko, Aaron, and Eric back again.) What kind of books would be helpful in expanding the Scion universe for your game? Any wish-fulfilling thoughts on topics?<br /> <br /> The two book topics that I would like to see is:<br /> <br /> 1. A book of Gods and Goddesses. There are other gods and goddesses in the pantheons that also can be used as divine parents for Scions. In the Pesdajet, Maat wasn't only a concept, she was also a Goddess of Order and wife to Thoth. There was also deities that were listed in the pantheon that were relegated to side blurbs like Anubis's son Wepawer and Horus's children, and weren't included like the hippo goddess of childbirth (I forget her name) and Bes, the dwarf god. There was a ton of Greek and Roman gods as well, like Morpheous (see thread on new purviews) and Terminus (Roman God of Paths), Eris (Goddess of Discord), and Nemesis (Goddess of Vengence). And who knows who was left out of First Edition that was part of a certain pantheon. A book detailing the minor gods and goddesses will expand on the flavor of Scions in general.<br /> <br /> 2. A book of other worlds or realities. Just like how the WoD has the shard book &quot;Mirrors&quot;, Scion could have a book detailing of other worlds that Scions can visit or other realities where things happened differently (kind of like a Scion version of the show Sliders.) Imagine if Zeus and the other deities were the ones locked in Tarturus as Titans and the Titans were the Olympian gods and goddesses. You could run into a version of yourself who's a Scion of Chronus, who can use the Time Purview. Imagine going into a reality where the pantheons war against each other to be dominate in a Pantheon War. James Lovegrove wrote about this in his godpunk novels Age of Ra, and Age of Aztec. Onyx Path could call these realities Twists (insert your &quot;What a Twist!&quot; joke here), because in the grand scheme of Fate, these different realities are essentially Twists of Fate. <br /> <br /> Any ideas for Onyx Path to use in future books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:46:25-08:00","id":46864,"title":"","content":"Your book of other worlds could be a supplement dealing specifically with Terra Incognita they'd like to include. As it is they were scattered all over Demigod and Ragnarok when they could have been one minibook. There could be a specific book about the titanrealms as well, allowing them to flesh them out more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T13:39:16-08:00","id":47034,"title":"","content":"I would throw such incredible amounts of money if the Scion example characters were Donnie and crew again","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:05:04-08:00","id":47668,"title":"","content":"A book of enemies would be good, also something that expands on birthrights and equipment. and whatnot. I usually tend to run campaigns that explore the fringes instead of mainline, even when I do not start out to do so; anything that actually goes into the concepts and relationships behind things helps in that kind of campaign. I am too new at Scion (I am just starting to get my first campaign campaign together in it) to know what else to suggest yet. <br /> <br /> While this is slightly off topic, another suggestion would be to introduce the pantheons and skill/power set in a more &quot;top down&quot; way in the main book by giving overviews first instead of just dumping right into the detailed god writeups and skills/powers lists, especially since some of the perviews are not quite what they sound like from the names. The current book makes it hard to pick a parent to fit a character concept without already knowing all the gods and the game systems well to begin with for example; not a problem with a Storyteller that is very familiar with the game to guide players during generation but more difficult than it could be for a group without any previous exposure to the game, not to mention being a bit of a plow for a new Storyteller since none of it correlates well until after the whole thing is read instead of building from general to specific over the course of reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T03:15:29-08:00","id":48040,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/New_Gods_1971_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Probably as a Shard, or &quot;Twist&quot; or whatever Alt. Universes call them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T04:20:44-08:00","id":48061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=48040#post48040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/New_Gods_1971_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Probably as a Shard, or &quot;Twist&quot; or whatever Alt. Universes call them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Green Ronin holds the license for DC RPGs at the moment, with their DC Adventures line for Mutants and Masterminds 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T05:10:55-08:00","id":48078,"title":"","content":"i would like to see: some rules for creating a fresh new Pantheon.<br /> <br /> an alternate Setting in wich the Pantheons fight each other instead of the Titans<br /> <br /> an post Ragnar\u00f6k/Titanomachy-Setting, in wich most of the famous and ruling gods are dead and scions taking their place,<br /> also with a lot more modernized theme ( god of Internet,etc.) and Political gameplay.<br /> <br /> a huge list of Scion characters who became Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","user":"DeadGuy","date":". 01-13-2014, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:39:14-08:00","id":49831,"title":"","content":"1) Book of Pantheons: One per Pantheon. This gives a brief history of the pantheon, splats for the major and minor players, heroes, and creatures of that pantheon. Unique advantages and disadvantages for being a member of the pantheon. Secrets, relics, artifacts. Duties, rules, expectations. This could also show 'sub pantheons', smaller cliques within the larger pantheon that you can join. I think one book might want to go into depth about making your own clique, and how to eventually get this made into its own pantheon.<br /> <br /> 1a) Actually, to expand on it some: I would love to see the codes for each pantheon. For example, I have a list of the laws of Ma'at - these are the things you say to Anubis as your soul is being weighed against a feather - and this pretty much defines what is expected from follows of the faith. I've also got the 'code' for the Greeks, and for the Romans, and of course, there's Bushido for the Japanese faith. I'm sure we can find similar things for other fails as well. That way, if you're playing someone from the Egyptian Pantheon, you'll be well aware of what your conduct is expected to be.<br /> <br /> 2) Terra Incognita: One per Pantheon. The realms that exist, what's expected there, what you're going to encounter, how it plays with your abilities. It should also provide the usual - additional creatures, heroes, monsters, artifacts, relics. Perhaps some abilities you can only get if you go there and do the proper quests / find the proper trainer. Discussing how to get around, what touchstones are and how they work, and ultimately, how to make your own.<br /> <br /> 3) I want to say 'a book of powers', but it goes a bit beyond that. I'd rather see, scattered through the various books, how to develop powers, make your own, alternate paths if such a thing will still be viable. I would also love to see something like V:tR's Devotions. What happens if you mix power X with power Y? What kind of effect will you get? I want to see the abilities of the scions be more fluid and less 'if you have Fire X, it does Y', with no room to wiggle.<br /> <br /> 4) Balance between Offence and Defence. I really really don't want to see 'One Attribute to Rule Them All'. (I'm looking at you, <i>Dexterity</i>). I really want to see a balance between Attributes, so that yes, if you <i>do</i> focus on one, you'll rock in that field, but that doesn't mean you'll rock in the other field. For example, Dexterity may make me rock in throwing and ranged combat, but it should not mean that I'll automatically do craptonnes of damage with every hit.<br /> <br /> 5) I <b>absolutely</b> want to see something concrete said about the setting itself. Is the 'canon' setting one where the gods have a lot more worship on Earth? Are they all secret cults? Is it more a mirror of our world until the scions peel back the layers? If an ogre goes rampaging through the streets, and a scion hurls a care at him, will people see exactly that, or will they try to explain it in a manner that makes sense for the mundane world, ala Percy Jackson? Will they freak out, or take pictures? Will the newspapers scream about terrorist attacks and be amazed, or will they say 'a demigod battles an ogre in the streets of Kanata today'..? I know people will want to run their own settings, of course, but I want to know what the 'base 0' setting is. Even V:tR has a base 0 that people can agree on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T00:29:44-08:00","id":50501,"title":"","content":"Something on how the world at large reacts and responds to a dude on the back of a flaming gold chariot drawn by a pair of onyx glass winged horses wreathed in flame with a spear made of hammered sunlight battling a thousand eyed titanic monstrosity down the streets of London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T01:38:46-08:00","id":50522,"title":"","content":"I think they say something like <br /> &quot;holy shit holy shit holy shit!&quot; a lot and then start worshipping that person as a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T01:45:59-08:00","id":50525,"title":"","content":"A book on titans - plots, monsters, mortal cults.<br /> <br /> A book on the parts of the overworld not controlled by the major pantheons. Little gods, legendary places, neutral beings, ruined and abandoned realms to explore.<br /> <br /> A scion vs. scion-esque book, covering things like wars between pantheons, how such things affect the mortal world, and of course, what happens should scions reveal themselves to the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T02:16:56-08:00","id":50540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=50522#post50522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they say something like<br /> &quot;holy shit holy shit holy shit!&quot; a lot and then start worshipping that person as a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then? Media coverage? How does...Spain react when that happens in London? What does the Vatican say when a South American feathered serpent lands on the roof of the Sistine Chapel? What happens to shipping lanes when the seas become flooded with aquatic Titanspawn? Do we get celebrity gossip magazines now folowing the latest exploits of Mark Odinson? Etc.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see some coherent thought put into how the life of the regular 9-5 office worker changes, how the rice farmer in India and Cambodia are affected, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T08:11:14-08:00","id":50695,"title":"","content":"There are infinite variables to all of your questions though. Those arent things that can just &quot;be answered.&quot; Lot of things could all happen depending on the story, the STs views, the themes of that chronicle, and how the pcs handle it. The possibilities are near endless. Its just not something that has a definitive, or even vaguely definitive answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T09:05:19-08:00","id":50731,"title":"","content":"Fair enough...<br /> <br /> Vague enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:29:14-08:00","id":50829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=50522#post50522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they say something like<br /> &quot;holy shit holy shit holy shit!&quot; a lot and then start worshipping that person as a god.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's just it. Would they?<br /> If society accepts the gods are active and walking around and doing stuff, that'll have an impact on society. That'll shape civilization more drastically than anyone might expect.<br /> On the other hand, if it isn't, you might start seeing organizations getting together to actually fight the gods as a very real threat, and you'll have cults springing up all over the place.<br /> <br /> Either of these, I think, is fine, <i>as long as it is spelled out clearly as what the setting is like</i>. I very much want to see 'this is the baseline setting, and here's what's going on'. If the gods have a 'masquerade' of sorts, then fine. If everything is laid out in the open, then fine as well, as long as it is consistent, and we see the actual consequences for what the setting is like, and how it impacts society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:32:40-08:00","id":50830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=50695#post50695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are infinite variables to all of your questions though. Those arent things that can just &quot;be answered.&quot; Lot of things could all happen depending on the story, the STs views, the themes of that chronicle, and how the pcs handle it. The possibilities are near endless. Its just not something that has a definitive, or even vaguely definitive answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there's infinite variables, and the game designers can narrow it down to just a few.<br /> <i>Civilization has always been aware of the gods. Street preachers call out for the faithful to follow in the footsteps of their patrons, temples to multiple pantheons exist in a number of cities, and the workers pray before heading to work each day. The border between some nations is a little tense, as some faithful see the worshippers of other pantheons as 'heretical'.</i><br /> <br /> I mean, that's just an off-the-cuff, but it at least paints some picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T11:50:04-08:00","id":50898,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't need definitive...the idea would be a source book that proposes a few different possible scenarios, laying some of the groundwork and ideas for the ST to springboard from, to propose ideas about things the ST may not have even considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T12:21:31-08:00","id":50937,"title":"","content":"I'm the other way. I want a canon setting. Whether or not I <i>use </i>it is not relevant. I want there to be a baseline 'this is Scion', so that at least people have the same page to be on when discussing the setting as a whole. When you make a 'generic no setting', you get into the same problem you get with other games (D&amp;D), where you look at the mechanics for the classes and such, and go <i>but why the hell does it work that way?</i> The flavour is drained from everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T14:52:29-08:00","id":51083,"title":"","content":"Oh don't get me wrong - Core Book, Core Setting - but the topic is about what books we'd like to see in the line. An additional splat that goes over the random additional details not covered by the core setting would rock (seriously, I don't think the core 4 books are going to talk much about how Scions in London are affecting world rice production and knock on effects to the poor rice farmers in Cambodia) but a book that goes into those kinds of random details and proposes alternate ways the upswing of Legend in the world could affect it would be great for me.<br /> <br /> I like having my PCs come off their high crushing the Titanspawn and then, a few sessions later see that their indiscriminate action cost the livelihoods of a dozen families, spurring them on to perhaps try and fight an injustice there...with more knock on effects. Hey, how many people prayed for a good harvest? Why can't the Scions of Mars (farming and war!) muck in once in a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe have it written as a host of 'News Articles', a few hundred words and a few pictures offering snippets of Scion/God/Titanspawn etc. activity told through the lens of the normal natural public and their media, try to use different styles from a Fashion Tips style article from a Celebrity Magazine that follows the latest fashions of Aphrodite, then have something in the vein of the Economist talking about how Scion activity in Malta has led to great opportunities for the investor willing to take a risk, etc. Snippets delivered in a fun, characterful way, using modern media to tell the equivalent of 'fireside stories' about the exploits of the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 01-16-2014, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T18:28:35-08:00","id":51270,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a book, maybe just a pdf, that gives more specifics to Fatebinding and the world's reaction to scions. Possibly even a few different takes on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T13:21:57-08:00","id":52713,"title":"","content":"I would love <b>Scion: Titanspawn</b> that gave us rules for playing and advancing Titanspawn characters. What happens when a <i>Medusae</i> get's her Legend to 4+ by her deeds, can a <i>Satyr </i>rise in infamy enough to become a Demigod and then even to Godhood to replace the fallen Pan? Titanspawn are a varied and untapped resource not only for the ST but players as well.<br /> <br /> Also I would like a book about the Titans that would give us more on them and categorize them more neatly to certain Pantheons so that there would be easier option for those who want to play single Pantheon games, that is games where one Pantheon is the true one the rest are just humanity's garbled twisted versions of them. That is to say that there would be Greek Titans and apart from the Greeks do the rest even need Titan enemies? The Gods do infight enough on their own generally and there are their own enemies, and yes these could be called Titans but in my opinion shouldn't, like Apep for example. Since the Pantheons are neatly represented without muddying the waters why not do the same with the Titans and other entities that oppose the Gods. Give each Pantheon it's own enemies from it's own myths and I dare say the game only get's better for it. For those who want all Pantheons to exists at the same time it gives even more enemies than we have currently, as the Titans of Scion 1st ed are multitasking as enemies of many Pantheons and with this divide every Pantheon would have it's own enemies, and for those who want one Pantheon to be &quot;correct&quot; they can have clearer, and again more, cut enemies that fit better with the actual myths.<br /> <br /> Well I admit the latter thing is just me daydreaming but the first book is something I really really would love to come to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T05:14:19-08:00","id":56051,"title":"","content":"I would like to see some guidelines to those who would like to run crossovers with either World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T10:27:35-08:00","id":56216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=56051#post56051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see some guidelines to those who would like to run crossovers with either World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions would pretty much wreck most WOD characters, at least to the best of my knowledge, would lose at low power levels to Exalted and beat high power level Exalted due to autosuccesses","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T11:15:32-08:00","id":56240,"title":"","content":"Re: settings. How Joe's put it is that there'll be a core of setting-agnostic stuff, as in 1e, but both Origins and Hero will provide some settings for groups to use. If people like them, they may do PDFs that further expand them, and/or PDFs that add some more settings.<br /> <br /> Not knowing what the settings are like beforehand, what public reaction is to the revelation of the gods will likely vary from setting to setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T12:52:47-08:00","id":56297,"title":"","content":"I think Scion is going to share Trinity's system, which will be a very different d10 system from what either World of Darkness uses. I don't think we're gunna have much official &quot;crossover&quot; material. As Guitarsniper says, the power scales just aren't balanced at all. WoD has very different themes and influences from Scion. It'd be plopping Superman into Lost Boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:13:25-08:00","id":56314,"title":"","content":"&quot;Superman into Lost Boys&quot; seems apt. And since I despise vampires anyway...hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T23:25:04-08:00","id":56599,"title":"","content":"Another factor complicating crossover is that now Scion and the Worlds of Darkness are owned by different companies (Scion is Onyx Path's, the WoDs are White Wolf/CCP's). Getting to use the WoDs in Scion would, I rather suspect, cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T10:02:08-08:00","id":56840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=56216#post56216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions would pretty much wreck most WOD characters, at least to the best of my knowledge, would lose at low power levels to Exalted and beat high power level Exalted due to autosuccesses</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Scions have as much or more of an advantage over mortals, yet mortal characters still have an important role to play in the setting even in relation to gods.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want so much to see all of the different kinds of characters &quot;balanced&quot; as to see how the various groups would coexist and interact. It sounds as though Scion: Origin is going to bring in a variety of weaker supernatural creatures; it would be nice to have the option of using some of the World of Darkness material to describe such beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:19:36-08:00","id":62424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46764-what-book-topic-would-you-like-to-see-in-scion-2e?p=56240#post56240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: settings. How Joe's put it is that there'll be a core of setting-agnostic stuff, as in 1e, but both Origins and Hero will provide some settings for groups to use. If people like them, they may do PDFs that further expand them, and/or PDFs that add some more settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>This interests me. If it is anything like the opening to V:tR (for example), I'm fine. I don't mind if most of the book is agnostic, but as long as there's something for me to look at, and take into consideration, then I'm fine with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T00:43:18-08:00","id":62764,"title":"","content":"This might not be worth a full book, but I'd really like to see the idea that becoming a God makes you a fundamental aspect of the universe to the point that your ascension basically rewrites the laws of physics. If a really nice scion ascends as the God of the Seas than the physical oceans might become nicer and less dangerous to sail or be cast adrift into.<br /> <br /> Further discussion on how to do this with all the incompatible Gods of the Seas would be necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T02:51:44-08:00","id":62811,"title":"","content":"For the WoD into Scion thing, I will probably end up transferring things I like from WoD into Scion. A lot of my WoD games are pretty gonzo anyhow, so....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}